{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1786504420,"nonce":"Q4VrCqDKX81Zgg64PBdnogcu/Ck=","target":"a30fb433d99e72295a334e42114cdea360edcb3ada1f9d05ff7aacdfd55df250","message":"**What is wrong.** `internal/alerts/domain/event.go` models `alert_events.type` as a closed value-object enum — 36 `EventType` values, an unexported `s string`, and `NewEventType` as the only parser. Four other packages then re-declare 18 of those same values as bare `string` constants and use the copies. The kernel type is never named outside its own module.\n\nCONTEXT.md §6: *\"Enums are `TEXT` + `CHECK` in SQL, closed value-object types in Go. No Postgres `ENUM` types.\"* The Go half of that rule is currently satisfied only inside `alerts/domain`.\n\n**The demonstration.** The four re-declaration sites, 18 literals in total:\n\n- `internal/alerts/service/seam.go:248-261` — 6 `group.*` constants, consumed by `internal/grouping/service/service.go:227,342,394,531,535,621`.\n- `internal/notification/repository/events.go:20-28` — 7 `notification.*` and `delivery.*` constants.\n- `internal/rules/service/service.go:35-42` — 3 `rule.*` constants.\n- `internal/enrichment/service/pipeline.go:38-43` — 2 `enrichment.*` constants.\n\n`internal/notification/service/view.go:165-180` adds 10 more of the same values as inline map keys.\n\nThe consequence is that 21 of the 36 `EventType` values — every `group.*`, `rule.*`, `enrichment.*`, `notification.*`, `delivery.*` and `source.*` — have zero references anywhere in the tree outside `event.go` itself, production and test alike. `AllEventTypes` documents itself as the source both the renderer and the DDL CHECK are generated from, so the list is not dead; but the identifiers are, and 18 of the 21 are dead specifically because a duplicate exists.\n\nTwo of the seam's own stated justifications are false as written. `seam.go:17-18` says *\"`alert_events` has exactly ONE writer, and it is in this module\"* — there are two production writers, `internal/alerts/repository/event.go:124` and `internal/notification/repository/events.go:79`, and the second is the module whose seven literals are listed above. `seam.go:30-31` says *\"Every signature here is deliberately built from primitives, uuid.UUID and db.TenantScope, so the caller needs no type from the alerts kernel\"* — `internal/grouping/service/service.go:12` already imports `alerts/domain` as `kernel` and calls `kernel.NewLabels` and `kernel.ComputeGroupKey` at lines 169 and 177. CONTEXT.md §5.2b sanctions exactly that import: *\"`internal/alerts/domain` is the SHARED DOMAIN KERNEL and is the *only* sanctioned cross-domain `domain` import\"*, and `.golangci.yml:22-24` grants it to every domain block as RULE K.\n\n**Why it matters.** A closed enum whose values are reachable as untyped strings is an open enum with extra steps. `GroupEventRequest.Type` is a `string` (`seam.go:40`) parsed by `NewEventType` at call time, so a typo in a caller is a runtime `KindValidation` error rather than a compile error — which is the entire property the value object was built to provide. The `notification/repository` copies are worse than the seam's: they are consumed by a repository that inserts into `alert_events` without going through `NewEvent` at all, so the §D.4 invariants `NewEvent` enforces are not enforced on that path. And when the enum next changes, the compiler will point at one file out of five.\n\n**Where.** `internal/alerts/domain/event.go:22-26` (the closed type), `:29-118` (the 36 values), `:130-147` (`AllEventTypes`); `internal/alerts/service/seam.go:17-18,30-31,40,248-261`; `internal/notification/repository/events.go:20-28,79`; `internal/rules/service/service.go:35-42`; `internal/enrichment/service/pipeline.go:38-43`; `internal/notification/service/view.go:165-180`.\n\n**Scope.** medium\n\n**Done when.** `domain.EventType` is the only Go spelling of an `alert_events.type` value: `GroupEventRequest.Type` is a `domain.EventType`, the 18 duplicate string constants are deleted, the `view.go` map is keyed by `EventType`, and every one of the 21 currently-uncalled values either has a production caller naming it or is removed from the enum and the DDL CHECK together. The two false claims in `seam.go` are corrected or the second `alert_events` writer is routed through the seam.","files":null}]}